  "prompt": "How many rows of subscription_events arrived, how many events do they hold, and how many rows are copies? These tables may hold errors. Some subscription events arrived twice: two rows of subscription_events are copies of one event when subscription_id, event_type, event_date and mrr_delta_local all match. Keep the row with the lowest event_id. Clean nothing else. Return one row with three columns, in this order: rows_arrived, events (once copies are removed) and copies (rows_arrived minus events). Any row order is fine.",
